clj (ds/defopen :file-input-stream\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/file_input_stream.cljc:151:#?(:cljd (ds/defopen :file-input-stream\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/file.cljc:341:(ds/defopen :file\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream/ringbuffer.cljc:414:(ds/defopen :ringbuffer\n  1130\t\n  1131\t\n  1132\t(defn published\n  1133\t  \"Construct a §5 published descriptor for one immutable covered-index\n  1134\t   manifest. content-store is a serializable DaoJing coordinate (map with\n  1135\t   :dao.jing/type); manifest-address is a segment content address.\n  1136\t   Validates like index/published-index but carries the schema type.\"\n  1137\t  [content-store manifest-address]\n  1138\t  (when-not (and (map? content-store) (keyword? (:dao.jing/type content-store)))\n  1139\t    (throw (ex-info \"published requires a DaoJing store coordinate\"\n  1140\t                    {:content-store content-store})))\n  1141\t  (when-not (jing/segment-address? manifest-address)\n  1142\t    (throw (ex-info \"published requires a manifest content address\"\n  1143\t                    {:manifest-address manifest-address})))\n  1144\t  {:dao.stream/type :dao.space.schema/published\n  1145\t   :dao.stream/bound {:manifest-address manifest-address}\n  1146\t   :dao.stream/comparator :dao.space.index/eavt\n  1147\t   :content-store content-store\n  1148\t   :manifest-address manifest-address})\n  1149\t\n  1150\t\n  1151\t#_{:clj-kondo/ignore [:unresolved-symbol :unresolved-var :private-call]}\n  1152\t\n  1153\t\n  1154\t(ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/published\n  1155\t            [descriptor]\n  1156\t            (let [{:keys [content-store manifest-address]} descriptor\n  1157\t                  expected (published content-store manifest-address)]\n  1158\t              (when-not (= expected descriptor)\n  1159\t                (throw (ex-info \"invalid schema/published descriptor\"\n  1160\t                                {:descriptor descriptor, :expected expected})))\n  1161\t              (let [r (ds/open! (index/published-index content-store manifest-address))]\n  1162\t                ;; The btree is lazily loaded from the store.  Eagerly force all\n  1163\t                ;; datoms now so the data is cached in memory.  When schema/current\n  1164\t                ;; later calls ds/close! (which closes the jing store) and then\n  1165\t                ;; interpret-view, the datoms delay is already realized and next()\n  1166\t                ;; reads from the cached vector — no store access needed.\n  1167\t                (ds/strict-vec r)\n  1168\t                r)))\nsrc/cljc/dao/stream.cljc:101:   (defmacro defopen\ncollab/1788948293243-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:611:(ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/published\ncollab/1788948293243-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:617:    (->PublishedSchemaRows rows)))\ncollab/1788948293243-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:620:`PublishedSchemaRows` is a small private record in `schema.cljc` implementing\ncollab/1788948293243-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:680:exercise `schema/published` through `ds/open!`/`schema/current`, exactly the\ncollab/1788948293243-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:693:  `:dao.space.schema/published` \"delegates to the `published-index`\ncollab/1788948293243-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r3.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:728:  Plus one addition: Phase 3's `PublishedSchemaRows`. Worth naming rather than\ndocs/design/dao.space.schema.md:551:`(ds/defopen :dao.space.schema/published …)` that delegates to the\ndocs/design/dao.space.schema.md:557:{:dao.stream/type :dao.space.schema/published\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
